4. Real-world interview queries
Imagine you have an orders table with order_id, order_date, and delivery_date.
Q1. Find orders placed in 2026.
SELECT *
FROM orders
WHERE order_date >= '2026-01-01'
  AND order_date < '2027-01-01';


This range-based approach can use an index on order_date more effectively than applying YEAR() to every row.
Q2. Find orders delivered within seven days.
SELECT *
FROM orders
WHERE DATEDIFF(delivery_date, order_date) <= 7;


This assumes both dates are populated and that you want to include any delivery completed in seven days or less.
Q3. Find orders placed in the current month.
SELECT *
FROM orders
WHERE order_date >= DATE_FORMAT(CURDATE(), '%Y-%m-01')
  AND order_date < DATE_ADD(
      DATE_FORMAT(CURDATE(), '%Y-%m-01'),
      INTERVAL 1 MONTH
  );


This works for a DATE or DATETIME column and covers the current calendar month.
Q4. Calculate a delivery deadline seven days after each order.
SELECT
    order_id,
    order_date,
    DATE_ADD(order_date, INTERVAL 7 DAY) AS deadline
FROM orders;

